roots:
Say what you will, and scratch my heart to find
The roots of last year’s roses in my breast;
I am as surely riper in my mind

My God is dark--like woven texture flowing,
A hundred drinking roots, all intertwined;
I only know that from His warmth I'm growing.

roofed:
The misted early mornings will be cold;
The little puddles will be roofed with glass.
The sun, which burns from copper into brass,

roofless:
Fell my house I built on sand;
Roofless, wounded, maimed by sin,
Fightings without and fears within:

root:
Tree of my life, Death's cruel foot
Hath crushed thee down to thy hidden root;
Nought shall restore thy glory fled . . .

roostin:
Snow 's a-fallin' on de medders, all erroun' me now is white,
But I 's still kep' on a-roostin' on de fence;
Isham comes an' feels my breas'bone, an' he hefted me las' night,
